<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nga Yaman Kan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1084</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nga Yaman Kan was the governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bago">Pegu</a> (Bago) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burma">Lower Burma</a> under the Pagan Kingdom, a boyhood companion of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sawlu">Sawlu</a>. In 1084 he rebelled, defeated the royal army and killed the captured Sawlu. The general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyansittha">Kyansittha</a> then crushed the revolt, and Nga Yaman Kan was killed while fleeing, leaving Kyansittha to take the throne of Pagan.</p></div>
